The stronger the wind, the faster the blades turn and the greater the electric power. But in a real turbine, this relationship is not simple:
• the blades start turning when the wind speed reaches 3 m/s;
• when the wind speed is 12 m/s, the power reaches its maximum value of 3 MW;
• for safety, in winds stronger than 12 m/s the blades are not allowed to turn any faster;
• when the wind speed reaches 25 m/s, the turbine is shut down.

Which graph best shows the relationship between wind speed and electric power according to these conditions?
